  "notes": [
    "booking.customer is stored as a human name string, not a foreign key to customer.id — production schema needs FK + join",
    "booking.chauffeur stores chauffeur.id as a string (empty when unassigned)",
    "chauffeur.vehicle stores vehicle.id as a string (empty when no assignment)",
    "review.vehicleClass stored as string, not FK — consider denormalization vs consistency",
    "all money values (coupons.value, surcharges.amounts, surcharges.pct, routes.economy/business/van, rates.baseFare/perKm/minFare) stored as strings with design-system placeholders (e.g., '000', '00', '0.00') — production must convert to numeric or decimal types",
    "settings.minAdvance and settings.cancelWindow are data-tok placeholders (empty strings in mock) — these are labelled TBC gaps awaiting real values",
    "profile.role stored as label string ('Admin role'), not enum — consider defining role enum",
    "review.locked is a computed boolean derived from whether the source is imported (google|tripadvisor|trustpilot = true, manual = false)",
    "id generation uses Base36 timestamps for pseudo-UUIDs except bookings (which use VT-<4-digit random>) and rates (which use klass name directly)",
    "RATE_DEFAULT_PAX hard-coded map: Economy/Business/First = 3 pax, Van = 8 pax",
    "surcharges.kind determines which field is active: amount-type uses .amounts, percent-type uses .pct, included-type uses neither"
  ]
}